Top-Level folder for the ElysianVMU project.


================
DIRECTORY LAYOUT
================
1) app - source directory for each front-end implementation of ElysianVMU emulator
	a. qt - source directory for EVMU using the Qt front-end (Windows, Mac, Linux, Raspberry Pi)
2) bin - Contains the BIOS image for testing/coding and a WIP analysis of everything we've figured out about the BIOS
3) build - Directory containing projects for building the codebase with different IDEs
	b. qtcreator - contains project file for building ElysianVMU using qtcreator
4) evmu-core - submodule containing the vanilla C emulator back-end, built upon libGyro
5) qtcreator - contains Qt project for building 

============
DEPENDENCIES
============
To build ElysianVMU, the following submodules must be checked out/initialized in the root directory:
1) evmu-core: vanilla C emulator back-end.
	a. libGyro - inner submodule within the evmu-core submodule that must also be initialized

